<title>USA: IPO FILING - Physicians' Specialty Corp.</title>
<headline>IPO FILING - Physicians' Specialty Corp.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Company Name	    Physicians' Specialty Corp</p>
<p>Stock symbol			ENTS.O</p>
<p>Estimated price range	   n/a</p>
<p>Total common shares to be offered 2.0 million</p>
<p>Shrs offered by company	 2.0 million</p>
<p>Shrs offered by shareholders  none</p>
<p>Shrs outstanding after IPO    5,328,725</p>
<p>Lead Underwriter    Barrington Capital Group L.P.</p>
<p>Underwriters over-allotment  300,000 shrs</p>
<p>Business: Atlanta, Ga.,-based company provides practice management servies to medical groups specializing in ear, nose and throat disorders.</p>
<p>Use of Proceeds: For working capital, including funding for future acquisitions; to repay its debt and that of Atlanta Ear, Nose &amp; Throat Associates P.C., which it is acquiring; to expand its information systems.</p>
<p>Financial Data in 000s:     1995		 1994</p>
<p>   - Net Revenues	    $9,492	     $8,020</p>
<p>   - Operating Income	 2,549		2,058</p>
